window.grammarSummary = "# 學測英文核心文法與句型總整理 (Grammar Review Guide)\n\n本手冊彙整了 **Unit 1 ~ Unit 16** 所有單元之核心文法重點，並依據語意與文法功能進行**分類歸納**。每個文法皆標示**來源篇章 (Unit)**、**高中課本冊數**、**核心結構**、**課文原句**、**文法說明**及**寫作實戰**，方便快速複習與交叉比對。\n\n---\n\n## 📌 學習導覽目錄 (Table of Contents)\n\n* 🔍 **[第一類：分詞片語與分詞構句 (Participle Clauses)](#第一類分詞片語與分詞構句-participle-clauses)**\n  * *包含句首分詞簡化、分詞後置修飾、伴隨狀態分詞、with 複合結構等*\n\n* 🔗 **[第二類：關係詞子句與副詞子句 (Relative & Adverbial Clauses)](#第二類關係詞子句與副詞子句-relative--adverbial-clauses)**\n  * *包含介係詞與關代、關係副詞 where、關係代名詞 What、非限定關係子句簡化等*\n\n* ⚖️ **[第三類：對比、並列與平行結構 (Contrast & Parallelism)](#第三類對比並列與平行結構-contrast--parallelism)**\n  * *包含並列名詞子句 that 保留、比較級修飾、Not only... but also、rather than、In contrast 對比等*\n\n* 💡 **[第四類：特殊動詞、片語與介係詞句型 (Special Verbs & Prepositions)](#第四類特殊動詞片語與介係詞句型-special-verbs--prepositions)**\n  * *包含雙重否定、完成式被動、倒裝句、虛受詞、be confined to、anything but 等*\n\n---\n\n## 第一類：分詞片語與分詞構句 (Participle Clauses)\n\n分詞（現在分詞 $V-ing$ 與過去分詞 $V-ed$）常用於簡化句子、作為形容詞修飾名詞，或是作為狀語引導從屬子句。此類句型是學測克漏字與寫作的超級重難點。\n\n### 1. 分詞片語引導的狀語從屬子句 (Participle Clauses as Adverbial) `[高中英文第四冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`V-ed / V-ing..., S + V`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 1** | **Held** every three to four years, the WBC is a tournament that brings together many of the world's best baseball players.<br>*(還原：Because the WBC is held every three to four years...)* |\n| **Unit 3** | **Nestled** along the beautiful Adriatic coast, Croatia is one of Europe's most appealing travel destinations.<br>*(還原：Because Croatia is nestled...)* |\n| **Unit 3** | **Dating** back to the 13th century, the city's iconic walls were famously featured in *Game of Thrones* and now rank among the country's most celebrated attractions.<br>*(還原：Which date back to... ➔ date back 無被動態，必用主動分詞 Dating)* |\n| **Unit 13** | **Dug** in beneath the sand, lugworms are able to stay underwater for more than eight hours during high tide.<br>*(還原：Since lugworms are dug in...)* |\n| **Unit 14** | **Located** at the northern end of our planet, the Arctic is a vast, icy ecosystem stretching across the Arctic Ocean and surrounding lands.<br>*(還原：Because the Arctic is located...)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：當從屬子句的主詞與主要子句主詞相同時，可省略連接詞與從屬子句主詞。若動詞為主動關係，變更為 **$V-ing$**；若為被動關係或狀態，變更為 **$V-ed$**。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *坐落於山頂的別墅擁有極佳的視野。*\n    ➔ **Nestled** on the hilltop, the villa has a great view.\n  * *這本書是由名教授寫的，深受學生歡迎。*\n    ➔ **Written** by a famous professor, the book is popular.\n\n---\n\n### 2. 分詞後置修飾名詞 (Noun Post-modification by Participles) `[高中英文第三冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`N + V-ed / V-ing`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 2** | They believed that the British government was violating their rights through policies like unfair taxation **imposed** without their consent.<br>*(還原：...taxation which was imposed without their consent)* |\n| **Unit 12** | Today, the Tower of London is a popular tourist destination, offering anyone **drawn** to royal history a chance to step back in time.<br>*(還原：...offering anyone who is drawn to royal history...)* |\n| **Unit 14** | Located at the northern end of our planet, the Arctic is a vast, icy ecosystem **stretching** across the Arctic Ocean and surrounding lands.<br>*(還原：...an ecosystem which stretches across...)* |\n| **Unit 16** | This is convenient for people with busy schedules, but it makes shopping a purely routine activity, **stripped of** the social element that many people value.<br>*(還原：...a purely routine activity which is stripped of the social element...)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：用以修飾先行名詞。可看作是「關係代名詞 ＋ $be$ 動詞」被省略後的簡化結果。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *站在門口的那位女孩是我的妹妹。*\n    ➔ The girl **standing** at the door is my sister.\n  * *他們不接受任何在壓力下做出的決定。*\n    ➔ They do not accept any decisions **made** under pressure.\n\n---\n\n### 3. 主動伴隨狀態的分詞構句 (Concomitant Participle Clause) `[高中英文第四冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`S + V..., V-ing...`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 5** | After graduation, Liu enrolled at UCLA, **majoring** in psychology.<br>*(還原：...enrolled at UCLA, and she majored in psychology)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：用於描述與主要動詞同時發生或伴隨發生的動作，常由對等連接詞簡化而來。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *他躺在沙發上，看著電視。*\n    ➔ He lay on the sofa, **watching** TV.\n\n---\n\n### 4. 形容詞/介係詞片語置於句首修飾 (Adjective / Prepositional Phrase as Modifier) `[高中英文第四冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`Adj-phrase, S + V...` / `N + born of + N`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 15** | **Native to** India, pepper has been traded for thousands of years.<br>*(還原：Because pepper is native to India, it has been...)* |\n| **Unit 8** | A discovery **born of** agricultural curiosity had been transformed into an instrument of modern warfare.<br>*(還原：A discovery which was born of agricultural curiosity...)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：形容詞片語可以簡化置於句首，修飾主句主詞的背景或狀態。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *由於對這個結果很滿意，他笑了。*\n    ➔ **Satisfied with** the result, he smiled.\n\n---\n\n### 5. 起源與根基結構 (Be Rooted in / Be Born of) `[高中英文第四冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`be rooted in + N`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 16** | Personally, my preference for traditional markets runs deep, **rooted in** warm childhood memories of visiting them with my grandmother.<br>*(還原：...runs deep, and it is rooted in warm childhood memories...)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：`rooted` 與 `born` 均以過去分詞的狀態修飾事物或概念的起源。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *她的成功根植於她堅持不懈的努力。*\n    ➔ Her success **is rooted in** her persistent hard work.\n\n---\n\n### 6. with + 受詞 + 受格補語的複合結構 (With + O + O.C.) `[高中英文第四冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`with + O + O.C. (V-ed / V-ing / Adj / Prep)`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 13** | Lugworm blood has already been proven highly effective in keeping human organs alive for transplants, with organs **stored** in the solution **able** to survive for days without damage.<br>*(說明：stored 作為過去分詞修飾 organs，而形容詞片語 able to... 作為第二個補語表示狀態)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：用以表達附帶狀態或原因。受詞 (organs) 與補語 (stored) 之間呈被動關係，故用過去分詞。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *由於雙眼被布矇住，他只能靠聽覺辨別方向。*\n    ➔ **With** his eyes **blindfolded**, he had to rely on his hearing.\n\n---\n\n## 第二類：關係詞子句與副詞子句 (Relative & Adverbial Clauses)\n\n關係詞（關係代名詞 $who/which/that$、關係副詞 $where/when$）用來連結句子。如何省略、前置與簡化為關係子句，是高二英文最核心的任務。\n\n### 1. 介係詞 ＋ 關係代名詞的前置與後置 (Preposition + Relative Pronoun) `[高中英文第三冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`Prep + which / whom` vs `N + [that] ... + Prep`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 5** | Just four years prior to her win, she had walked away from figure skating entirely, unsure whether she would ever return to the sport she had once **devoted herself to**.<br>*(後置：sport [that] she had devoted herself to — 關係代名詞可省略)* |\n| **Unit 5** | ...unsure whether she would ever return to the sport **to which** she had once devoted herself.<br>*(前置對照：to which 介係詞前置，關係代名詞不可省略，亦不可用 that)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：當關係子句中的動詞包含介係詞時，介係詞可以搬到關係代名詞前方。注意 `to that` 是錯誤文法。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *這就是我一直在尋求的機會。*\n    ➔ This is the opportunity **for which** I have been looking. (或：...the opportunity **[that]** I have been looking **for**.)\n\n---\n\n### 2. 關係副詞 where 引導的非限制性形容詞子句 (Relative Adverb \"Where\") `[高中英文第二/三冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`N, where + S + V`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 7** | One-stop shopping—**where** everything was available under one roof—became a dominant business model.<br>*(說明：where 引導非限制性子句，補充說明一站式購物的商業概念)* |\n| **Unit 14** | Polar bears spend much of their time on sea ice, **where** they patiently hunt seals.<br>*(說明：where 補充說明 sea ice 上的環境與北極熊狩獵海豹的行為)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：`where` 作為關係副詞，相當於 `in/on/at which`，引導非限制性子句時，主要用於對前面提到的地點或環境進行「補充說明」，其前面須加逗號（或破折號）。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *我們搬進了新大樓，那裡的生活非常方便。*\n    ➔ We moved into a new building, **where** life is very convenient.\n\n---\n\n### 3. 關係代名詞 What 引導的名詞子句當主詞 (Noun Clause with \"What\") `[高中英文第三冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`What (+ S) + V + V(單數)...`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 6** | **What** began as a small cultural experiment soon set the stage for the famous Avignon Festival.<br>*(說明：What 引導名詞子句當主詞，等同於 The thing that began...)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：`What` 是複合關係代名詞，等於 `The thing(s) which/that`。引導名詞子句當主詞時，後續的動詞應搭配**單數**。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *他所說的話讓每個人都笑了。*\n    ➔ **What** he said **made** everyone laugh.\n\n---\n\n### 4. 非限制性關係子句與分詞簡化 (Which vs V-ing) `[高中英文第四冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`..., which shows that...` ➔ `..., showing that...`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 9** | Extreme weather events have become increasingly frequent, **showing that** climate change is hitting harder.<br>*(還原：..., which shows that climate change is hitting harder)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：`, which + V` 可簡化為 `, V-ing`。代表前面整件事所產生的必然結果或隨附狀態。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *他通過了考試，這讓每個人都很驚訝。*\n    ➔ He passed the exam, **surprising** everyone. (或：..., **which surprised** everyone.)\n\n---\n\n## 第三類：對比、並列與平行結構 (Contrast & Parallelism)\n\n大考寫作非常看重句子的對稱美與連貫性。並列名詞子句、比較級修飾及轉折連接詞的對稱，是寫作高分的秘訣。\n\n### 1. 並列名詞子句中連接詞 that 的保留規則 (Parallel Noun Clauses with \"that\") `[高中英文第三冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`S + V + (that) S1+V1, and that S2+V2.`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 2** | In the declaration, Jefferson wrote **that** \"all men are created equal\" and **that** they have the right to \"life, liberty, and the pursuit of happiness.\"<br>*(說明：並列了兩個由 wrote 所引導的名詞子句，第二個 that 必須保留以防混淆)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：當同一個及物動詞後面並列兩個 `that` 引導的名詞子句時，為了防止語意混淆，**第一個 `that` 可省，但第二個 `that` 必須保留**。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *老師說我們應該早點睡，且我們不該熬夜。*\n    ➔ The teacher said (that) we should sleep early and **that** we shouldn't stay up late.\n\n---\n\n### 2. 比較級的加強修飾副詞 (Modifiers for Comparatives) `[高中英文第一/二冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`much / even / far / still / a lot + 比較級`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 4** | These are **much more** comfortable.<br>*(對照：These are much cheaper than the other ones.)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：用以強調差異的副詞。**絕對不可使用 *very* 來修飾比較級**（例如：*very cheaper* 是錯的）。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *今天的考試比昨天的簡單多了。*\n    ➔ Today's exam is **even easier** than yesterday's.\n\n---\n\n### 3. Not only... but also... 的平行結構 (Parallelism with \"Not Only... But Also...\") `[高中英文第二冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`not only A but (also) B`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 6** | Artists and audiences arrive from around the world, and performances are held **not only** in traditional venues **but also** in cafés, gardens, and even churches.<br>*(說明：A 和 B 皆為地方介係詞片語 in...，結構對稱)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：A 與 B 的**語法結構與詞性必須完全對稱**。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *凱莉不僅聰明，而且非常勤奮。*\n    ➔ Kelly is **not only** intelligent **but also** extremely diligent.\n\n---\n\n### 4. 轉折連詞 rather than 的平行對稱 (Rather Than) `[高中英文第三冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`S + V + rather than + V-ing/V/N`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 10** | When it comes to toppings, you should focus on finding combinations you enjoy **rather than** trying everything at once.<br>*(說明：enjoying... 與 trying... 呈動名詞結構平行對稱)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：意為「而不是……；與其……不如……」。前後引導的成分也需要具有**平行對稱的詞性**。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *他選擇去搭火車，而不是搭飛機。*\n    ➔ He chose to go by train **rather than** fly.\n\n---\n\n### 5. 對比副詞 In contrast 與 On the contrary 的辨析 (In Contrast) `[高中英文第二/三冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`S + V. In contrast, S2 + V2.`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 16** | Supermarkets, **in contrast**, offer a quieter and more organized experience, where customers browse shelves independently with minimal interaction.<br>*(說明：將超市與傳統市場的購物體驗進行客觀對比)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：`in contrast` 用於**對比兩個不同客觀事實**；而 `on the contrary` 則是用於**駁斥對方的預期**（意為「正好相反、根本不是這樣」）。這是大考極愛測試的微言大義。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *他很外向；相比之下，他妹妹很害羞。*\n    ➔ He is outgoing; **in contrast**, his sister is very shy.\n\n---\n\n## 第四類：特殊動詞、片語與介係詞句型 (Special Verbs & Prepositions)\n\n本類別彙整了高頻的句型結構，如雙重否定、倒裝句、虛受詞，以及容易混淆的介係詞用法。\n\n### 1. 雙重否定與強調語氣 (Double Negative) `[高中英文第一/三冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`have no shortage of + N`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 1** | This year's WBC had **no shortage of** surprising moments.<br>*(語意：...had plenty of surprising moments. 有非常多令人驚奇的時刻)* |\n\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *這座城市不乏好玩的景點與美味餐廳。*\n    ➔ This city **has no shortage of** fun attractions and delicious food.\n\n---\n\n### 2. 尚未發生的被動語態 (Present Perfect Passive with \"yet\") `[高中英文第二冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`S + have yet to be + V-ed`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 1** | The timing and locations of the next WBC **have yet to be** determined.<br>*(語意：...have not been determined yet. 尚未被確定)* |\n\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *該新計劃的細節尚未被公佈。*\n    ➔ Details of the new project **have yet to be announced**.\n\n---\n\n### 3. be supposed to 的義務與預期用法 (Supposed to V) `[高中英文第二/三冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`S + be supposed to + V-原型`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 4** | Wait, are we **supposed to** tip at food courts?<br>*(語意：Are we expected/obligated to tip... 預期或義務要做某事)* |\n\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *學生本來就不應該在課堂上睡覺。*\n    ➔ Students **are not supposed to** sleep in class.\n\n---\n\n### 4. 程度與結果句型 to such an extent that (To Such an Extent That) `[高中英文第四冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`to such an extent that + S + V` / `little more than`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 6** | Over time, however, the festival has expanded far beyond its original stage, **to such an extent that** the entire city of Avignon gets turned into a lively center for performing arts.<br>*(語意：擴大到「整個城市都變成表演中心」的程度)* |\n| **Unit 7** | For many people, shopping is **little more than** a daily chore.<br>*(語意：僅僅是、只不過是)* |\n\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *暴風雨增強到如此程度，以致於所有航班都被取消了。*\n    ➔ The storm grew **to such an extent that** all flights were canceled.\n\n---\n\n### 5. 限制與侷限介係詞片語 be confined to (Be Confined to) `[高中英文第三/四冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`S + be confined to + N/V-ing` / `be prone to + N/V-ing`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 8** | Galston's work may have seemed **confined to** the quiet world of plant biology, but history had other plans.<br>*(說明：confined to... 侷限於 quiet world...)* |\n| **Unit 9** | Spending too much time in the sun makes you **prone to** sunburn.<br>*(說明：prone to... 易於、有……傾向)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：其中的 `to` 皆為**介係詞**，後續須接名詞或動名詞。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *他因為生病而被限制在床上（臥床）。*\n    ➔ He was **confined to** bed because of illness.\n\n---\n\n### 6. faced with 與 in the face of 的對照 (Facing Challenges) `[高中英文第四冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`Faced with + N` (分詞) vs `In the face of + N` (介係詞)\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 9** | **In the face of** global warming, everyone should take action to protect the environment.<br>*(說明：In the face of 作為介係詞片語，引導主動/客觀環境)* |\n| **Unit 9** | **Faced with** financial difficulties, the company cut jobs.<br>*(對照：Faced with 為被動分詞，用以表示主語主動面臨的處境)* |\n\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *面對財務困難，公司決定裁員。*\n    ➔ **Faced with** financial difficulties, the company cut jobs.\n  * *面對危險，他保持冷靜。*\n    ➔ **In the face of** danger, he remained calm.\n\n---\n\n### 7. anything but 與 nothing but 的對照 (Anything But vs Nothing But) `[高中英文第三冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`anything but + Adj/N` (絕非/一點也不) vs `nothing but + N/V` (僅僅是/只有)\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 11** | Space exploration may still feel distant, but its impacts are **anything but** distant.<br>*(說明：絕非遙遠)* |\n\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *他的回答絕非誠實。*\n    ➔ His answer was **anything but** honest.\n  * *他整天只會抱怨。*\n    ➔ He did **nothing but** complain all day.\n\n---\n\n### 8. 介係詞片語與分詞置於句首的倒裝 (Inversion) `[高中英文第四冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`Prep-phrase + be + S` / `V-ing/V-ed + be + S`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 12** | **Among the most famous were** Anne Boleyn and Lady Jane Grey, both former queens who were eventually executed on the tower grounds.<br>*(說明：Among the most famous 地方介係詞片語置於句首，動詞 were 倒裝至主詞前)* |\n| **Unit 12** | **Guarding the tower are** the famous Yeoman Warders, commonly called Beefeaters, who wear traditional red uniforms and share fascinating stories about the building's colorful past with visitors every day.<br>*(說明：現在分詞 Guarding the tower 置於句首，動詞 are 倒裝至主詞前)* |\n\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *山腳下坐落著一個寧靜的小村莊。*\n    ➔ **At the foot of the mountain lies** a peaceful village.\n  * *抽屜裡藏著那把丟失的鑰匙。*\n    ➔ **Hidden in the drawer is** the lost key.\n\n---\n\n### 9. 虛受詞句型 Legend has it that (Legend Has It That) `[高中英文第三/四冊]`\n\n* **核心結構**：`Legend / Rumor / Word + has it + that-子句`\n\n| 來源單元 | 完整課文原句與語意還原對照 |\n| :---: | :--- |\n| **Unit 12** | **Legend has it that** if the ravens ever leave, both the tower and the kingdom will fall.<br>*(說明：it 為虛受詞，指代後續的完整 that 從屬子句)* |\n\n* **文法解析**：`it` 作為**虛受詞**，指代後面 `that` 引導的完整子句。\n* **寫作實戰**：\n  * *傳說這個湖裡住著一隻神秘的怪物。*\n    ➔ **Legend has it that** a mysterious monster lives in this lake.\n";